# D4 "biting" instance: a chain-graph LCN whose strong extension is LOOSE because
# of a CROSS-FAMILY sentence (scheme D4, docs/tighter_approximation.tex).
#
# Structure: A is the root; B and C are independent children of A, so the
# families are P(A), P(B|A), P(C|A). The sentence P(B and C) <= 0.05 has scope
# {B,C}, which is a subset of NO single family scope -> it is cross-family.
#
# The free product (strong extension) can pick high P(B|A) and high P(C|A)
# vertices simultaneously, reaching P(B and C) ~ 0.92 -- grossly violating the
# 0.05 bound. That joint is in the strong extension but NOT in the true LCN set.
# Credal VE with coupling="cross-family" forbids it: e.g. P(B | C=1) collapses
# from [0.0375, 0.9625] (coupling off) to [0.0375, 0.0375].
#
# Note: the LMC assertion (B _||_ C | A) is structurally satisfied by any
# product joint, so it is NOT what makes this instance loose -- the sentence is.
A1: 0.4 <= P(A) <= 0.6
B1: 0.1 <= P(B | A) <= 0.3
C1: 0.2 <= P(C | A) <= 0.5
BC: 0.0 <= P(B and C) <= 0.05
